      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Bank Findex number

Gender Corporate Scorecard Indicator Results:

Number of women using payment services: 11.6 million
Number of women using debt financing: 1.7 million

*The program, while focused on increasing women&apos;s use of payment services, has also led many to adopt other financial services like debt financing. Global Findex 2024 shows 15% of Indonesian women use debt services. Since the program began, an estimated 1.7 million more women have started using debt financing, indicating a significant expansion in women&apos;s access to credit. This figure is derived by applying the 15% Findex indicator (&#x201c;borrowed from a formal institution or via mobile money&#x201d;) to the rise in digital payment use among Indonesia&apos;s adult female population.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="Female: 43; Male: 42"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
